# Defect 2261, 2026-10-29 (panel 232's spec-warden, its table of shapes, and
# its completeness critic, R15 (b)). Symptom: `add2(b: "xy", a: 1)` over
# `add2(a: i64, b: str)` was refused four times, a `wrong_label` at each label
# and a `type_mismatch` at each value held to the type of its position, for
# one mistake. Cause: each label was read alone, and each value checked
# against its position. Now the two labels, which name each other's
# positions, are one order: told once at the first of them, naming the order
# declared and the order written, the values' messages one note inside it;
# Part 11's control arm, which drops `wrong_label`, says those two as it
# always did. The fix writes the values in the order declared, each with its
# label, `certain` here since both are literals. The call written so is left
# alone, and the program written so prints `xy1` (this Mac, 2026-10-29).
function add2(a: i64, b: str) -> str
    return b + a.to_str()

function main()
    print(add2(b: "xy", a: 1))  #~ wrong_label
    print(add2(a: 1, b: "xy"))
